## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical mastery of cross-service coordination using Saga, CQRS, and event sourcing in realistic e-commerce workflows. It emphasizes long-running process handling, compensation, and replay-safe state.

## Key Concepts

- Saga state machine with compensations for long-running business processes
- Event sourcing and CQRS read/write separation
- Idempotency, correlation IDs, and versioning to handle retries and out-of-order events
- Compensation patterns (ReleaseInventory, RefundPayment) and failure healing
- Snapshotting to bound event stores and speed reads

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator tick (high-level)
function onEvent(state, event) {
  if (state.orderId !== event.orderId) return state
  switch (event.type) {
    case 'CartVerified':
      return { ...state, currentStep: 'InventoryReserved' }
    case 'InventoryReserved':
      return { ...state, currentStep: 'PaymentHeld' }
    case 'PaymentFailed':
      // trigger compensations
      return { ...state, compensations: ['ReleaseInventory','OrderRollback'] }
    case 'OrderCommitted':
      return { ...state, currentStep: 'Completed' }
    default:
      return state
  }
}
```

